    description: "Unlimited."
  - name: "Breath Weapon: Ink Cloud"
    description: "It spews a dark liquid like an octopus''s ink. Above water the ink becomes a dense black cloud filling a 30x30x30 foot (9x9x9 m) area for 1D4 melee rounds. Everyone inside the magical darkness fights blind until out of it: -10 to strike, parry, dodge and every other combat move. It is ink, not smoke, so infrared and passive nightvision goggles do not see through it and neither does Nightvision. Underwater the cloud covers twice the area, with the same duration and effect."
  - name: "Camouflage Quick Change"
    description: "Like an octopus it shifts its skin color and pattern to match its surroundings. One change takes a single melee action/attack and may be made as often as desired. While in use it adds +10% to Prowl and Tailing."
  - name: "Chemoreceptors"
    description: "Taste sensors in the mouth pick up tiny changes in the salt and chemical content of the water. Identify chemicals by taste 72% +1% per level of experience; track by taste 72% +2% per level of experience, range one mile (1.6 km)."
  - name: "Metamorphosis"
    description: "It can become any kind of animal or humanoid no smaller than a wolf and no larger than itself, for two hours per level of experience. The shape has two legs and two arms unless the creature copied has more limbs, to a limit of eight."
  - name: "Natural Weapons"
    description: "Damage is as per Supernatural P.S. The bladed tail does 6D6+12 M.D.; a blunt tail strike does punch damage, and a power tail strike doubles it but uses two melee actions. Bite 1D6x10 M.D. A tentacle can grab and hold, or squeeze and crush for up to 3D6 M.D. per squeeze, each squeeze counting as one melee attack. The book prints these once and does not give the hatchling smaller figures."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any. The book says most Octo Dragons are Diabolic (25%), Miscreant (40%), Aberrant (10%) or Anarchist (15%), but some are merely selfish and a few are good - and even those are short-tempered and quick to violence."
  - "Speed: 3D6 slithering on its belly or crawling on its tentacles, and 1D6+18 swimming (20 mph/32 km or 17 knots). Swimming does not tire it."
  - "Attacks per melee: four physical attacks per melee round, or two by magic."
  - "The +1 to initiative becomes +2 in water."
  - "+1 on all saving throws other than Horror Factor (which is +3)."
  - "VULNERABILITIES: it does not like fire. Ordinary fire does half its damage as mega-damage (a fire doing 4D6 S.D.C. does 2D6 M.D. to it), while M.D. plasma, M.D. fire and magical fire do double damage. It also hates captivity, turning furious and violent - thrashing and bellowing until it is exhausted."
  - "MAGIC: born with a full understanding of magic but knows NO spells at level one. It can learn magic, and can use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical weapons and devices. Under the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules the book points to (p.158), spells are learned by the usual means from second level - by third level the hatchling has 2D4+2 spells from levels 1-3, another 2D4+2 by fifth level from levels 3-8, and 3 new spells per level thereafter up to its own level. Two spells may be cast per melee round, and it gains +1 to spell strength at level nine. Those counts are dice-valued, which a spell schedule cannot hold, so they are recorded here."
  - "PSIONICS: a Master Psychic. Death Trance, Meditation and Mind Block, plus five Physical powers of choice; one new Physical power at each new level of experience, and Radiate Horror Factor at level 12."
  - "On S.D.C. worlds a hatchling has 240 Hit Points, 2D6x10+80 S.D.C. and a Natural A.R. of 9 in place of its M.D.C."
  - "Size: an adult is 30-40 feet (9.1 to 12.2 m) from snout to where the tentacles end, plus 90-100 feet (27.4 to 30.5 m) of tail; the head is 8-10 feet (2.4 to 3 m) across and each tentacle 30-40 feet (9.1 to 12.2 m) long. Weight 30-50 tons. The book prints no separate hatchling size."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Magic Knowledge: without being taught it can work any Techno-Wizard device, recognise and use other magic weapons, read magic and use scrolls, and it recognises magic circles and enchantment at 40% +3% per level of experience. It senses ley lines and nexus points within 20 miles (32 km), and other dragons - even ones disguised by metamorphosis - on sight out to 4000 feet (1219 m). The sensing gives nearness and general direction, never an exact spot."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Weapons and Equipment: it can use any kind of weapon, and wears little clothing or mega-damage armor except as a disguise in humanoid form. It mostly counts on what it was born with, its magic and its psionics."
  - "From the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules (p.156-159) the book defers to: a hatchling behaves like a child of four to seven and must settle on a definitive alignment at level three; it does not need to eat or drink; it can never take cybernetics or bionics, which its bio-regeneration pushes back out; and under 100 years old it cares little for wealth, though it is always drawn to magic items."
side_effects: "ADULT OCTO DRAGON (not playable; the class stores the hatchling). Attributes I.Q. 2D6+16, M.E. 2D6+16, M.A. 2D6+8, P.S. 2D6+32, P.P. 2D6+16, P.E. 2D6+16, P.B. 1D6+6, Spd 3D6+10 on land (15 mph/24 km); the swimming Spd is printed as 2D6+20 for an average swim speed of 2D6+36 (around 30 mph/48 km or 26 knots). M.D.C. 2D4x1,000+1,600, +1D4x1,000 for an ancient (S.D.C. worlds: 5D6x10+160 Hit Points, 3D6x100 S.D.C., Natural A.R. 12). Horror Factor 15. P.P.E. 2D4x100+160. I.S.P. 2D6x10+16 + M.E., +10 per level; all Physical powers plus Radiate Horror Factor. Nine physical or psionic attacks per melee round, or four by magic. +1 on Perception Rolls, +4 initiative (+6 in water), +8 strike and parry, +8 disarm and entangle, +3 dodge, +6 pull punch, +2 roll with impact, +8 vs Horror Factor, +2 on all other saves. Magic: Wizard/Spell Invocations as a Ley Line Walker (90%), Ocean Magic (6%), or Necromancy or other dark magic (4%), about 3D6+16 spells; it avoids magic that links it to another being, so no Warlock or Shifter. Life span 1D6x1,000+1,600 years, some reaching 9,000. NPC level: 2D4 for adults, 1D4 for hatchlings."
extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 216-218 (cache p217-p219;
  cache page = printed + 1). Cache p218 and p219 carry known digit swaps, so
  every figure was read off 170-dpi renders of both columns of both pages; the
  text layer on those pages also runs its paragraphs out of order.

  Section heading: "Sea Dragons" (printed 208). A race, so no men_of_arms
  line is needed: the class states mdc_base.

  WHAT THE BOOK DEFERS TO RIFTS ULTIMATE EDITION, AND WHAT WAS REUSED.
  The entry says "Hatchling player characters start at level one" and twice
  sends the reader to Rifts Ultimate Edition p.156 for playing a dragon
  hatchling. Taken from the published dragon-hatchling-flame-wind class, not
  from this book:
  1. xp_table - the Rifts Ultimate Edition dragon ladder, copied from
     dragon-hatchling-flame-wind. This entry prints no ladder; the Leviathan
     in the same section (printed 209-210) says to use the Dragon Experience
     Table. Rifts Ultimate Edition''s Experience Tables (printed 295) head
     this ladder "Dragon Hatchling & Adult Dragon", and its hatchling
     section (printed 158) says to use the Dragon R.C.C. for level
     advancement.
  2. The spell-learning progression in the MAGIC restriction, and the last
     restriction line (alignment at level three, no need to eat, no
     cybernetics, money). This book prints only "know no spells at Level
     One ... can learn magic and use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical
     weapons and devices".
  3. The Magic Knowledge and Weapons and Equipment restriction lines, and
     "two spells per melee round, +1 to spell strength at level nine" in the
     MAGIC line. Rifts Ultimate Edition printed 158 prints all three in its
     general Dragon Hatchling section, as rules for every hatchling (the
     cache prints the spell strength figure as "+f"; it is +1).
  NOT reused: Rifts Ultimate Edition''s skill scheme (instinctive skills at
  98%, Secondary Skills, Special Areas of Interest). This entry prints its own
  "R.C.C. Skills (Hatchling)" list, which is what is stored.

  WHAT THE BOOK PRINTS AND WHAT WAS STORED.
  1. Skills: 14 named skills with a printed bonus; each base is the catalog
     base plus that bonus. "Pilot: Sail Boats" is held as Boat: Sail Type,
     "Underwater Navigation" as Navigation: Underwater, "Literate in
     Dragonese/Elven" as Literacy: Dragonese/Elven, "Lore: Demons and
     Monsters" as Lore: Demons & Monsters. "Interrogation" was matched to the
     Espionage row of that exact name (30%), not Interrogation Techniques.
  2. "A total of five skill selections from ... Aquatic, Communication,
     Rogue, Technical, Wilderness and W.P." is stored as a five-pick choice group
     in occ_skills with bonus 0. The catalog has no Aquatic category: the book''s
     Aquatic Skills list (printed 54) is spread over Technical, Wilderness,
     Horsemanship, Science, Medical and Pilot Related, so Horsemanship,
     Science and Medical are named with `only` lists holding the Aquatic
     skills filed there. Left out: Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter (the Serpent
     Hunter''s own) and Navigation: Underwater (Pilot Related; already an
     R.C.C. skill here). A single { name: "Aquatic", only: [...] } entry was
     tested and is refused by categoryAllows: a cross-category `only` is
     admitted only when the group also lists the skill''s real category.
  3. "Magically understands and speaks all languages at 85%" is stored as
     Language: All (magical) at 85 with no per-level gain.
  4. Attacks: "Four physical attacks per melee round or two by magic" is
     stored as attacks_base 4. The hatchling line, unlike the adult''s, does
     not say "or psionic".
  5. "+1 on all other saving throws" is stored as +1 on each of the fourteen
     other d20 saves the sheet draws (the percentile coma/death save is left
     alone), following dragon-hatchling-asama-tatsu, and is also kept as a
     restriction line.
  6. Initiative +1 is stored; "(+2 in water)" is conditional and is prose.
  7. Horror Factor 11 is stored in horror_factor.
  8. The S.D.C.-world figures (240 Hit Points, 2D6x10+80 S.D.C.) are stored in
     hit_points_base and sdc_base as the flame-wind model does; Natural A.R. 9
     is prose.
  9. Psionics: one Physical power per new level is written as a schedule entry
     per level, because a level-12 entry for Radiate Horror Factor is needed
     beside it. Radiate Horror Factor is a Super power; the level-12 entry
     names it outright.
  10. Spd stores the land figure (3D6); swimming Spd 1D6+18 is prose.
  11. Adult and ancient figures are prose only (side_effects).

  BOOK SLIPS.
  - Printed 218, Vulnerabilities & Weaknesses: the example reads "does 2D6
    M.D. to the Hydros Dragon". It sits inside the Octo Dragon entry and is
    taken as the Octo''s.
  - Printed 217, adult swimming Spd: "2D6+20 for an average swim speed of
    2D6+36". Two formulas in one sentence; quoted as printed, not resolved.
  - Printed 218: Mega-Damage and the natural abilities do not separate adult
    from hatchling. Stored once, as printed.
  - Printed 218: the heading "Magic Knowledge of an Adult: Adult:" repeats
    itself, and "Camouflage Quick Change" is the cache''s "Ouick".
---

## Lore

The Octo Dragon looks less like a dragon than like an enormous eel that has
borrowed an octopus''s limbs: a long serpentine body, a huge head with a double
row of sword-length teeth, a ridge of spines down the back, a tail ending in a
blade, and eight tentacles where legs and wings ought to be. Its skin changes
color and pattern at will, so it can be nearly any shade, though the resting
color is thought to be a pale brown-gray with pink beneath. Some scholars take
it for a creature from another dimension or an escaped experiment of the Lord
of the Deep; other dragons say they sense it as one of their own.

By reputation it is a bully. Most are short-tempered, aggressive and cruel,
treat weaker beings as prey or toys, and end up as generals for the Lord of
the Deep, as neighbors of the Splugorth, or as the self-declared king or god
of some frightened island or undersea settlement. A few are only selfish and a
few are genuinely good, and a player''s hatchling may be any of these - but
even a kind Octo Dragon has a quick temper.

It is a slow swimmer for a sea dragon and afraid of fire, and it cannot stand
being confined.

## GM Notes

The hatchling fights with reach and control rather than raw speed: eight
grabbing arms, strong parry, disarm and entangle bonuses, an ink cloud that
blinds everything inside it (Nightvision included), and a skin that hides it
as often as it likes for one action.

Fire is the lever against it. Even ordinary flame hurts it as mega-damage,
and plasma or magical fire does double. The book prints one set of natural
weapon damage for adult and hatchling alike; a 1D6x10 M.D. bite and a 6D6+12
M.D. tail blade are a lot for a first-level character, so decide before play
whether the hatchling uses them as printed.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-octo');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-octo';

